{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"goblin_totem","model_identifier":"goblin_totem","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# goblin_totem\n\nGoblin totem: a crooked pole hung with green-glowing hexstones on cords and skulls, a hide banner and crude paint.\n\n- Footprint: 2 x 2 columns (32 x 32 units, 0.90 x 0.90 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -18..18, y 0..116, z -10..10 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 18, construction_0 3, construction_33 4, construction_66 3, ruined 6 (10 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 8 x 116 x 8 centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `goblin_totem_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `goblin_totem_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_goblin_totem` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n"},"resolution":{"width":64,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"mound","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_orde